# Skill: tdd-enforce

> Auto-installed by `genasis attach` under `.claude/genasis/skills/tdd-enforce/`.
> The skill is a thin contract — it points at GENASIS.md and the relevant
> sections of `blueprint.md` rather than restating them.

## When to invoke
Red-Green-Refactor sequence; unit/integration/E2E ownership matrix.

## What I should do
1. Read `GENASIS.md` first.
2. If this skill is about an external system (Plane, Mattermost, DB),
   check the corresponding section of the per-role overlay fence in my
   own agent file.
3. Use the **direct API helpers** (or `genasis` CLI subcommands) rather
   than re-implementing protocol logic.
4. On any state change, post to the Mattermost issue thread; on any
   destructive op, refuse without explicit confirmation.

## Anti-patterns
- Restating the lifecycle locally (drifts from GENASIS.md).
- Using admin tokens when a role-scoped PAT is available.
- Issuing schema-modifying SQL outside of `genasis db migrate`.
